{"id": "portal-idempotency", "question": "How does the portal preserve a checkout attempt across retries?", "mode": "ask", "reference": "The portal stores the Idempotency-Key and checkout payload in tab-scoped sessionStorage and sends the key as a header.", "reference_kind": "factual_documentation", "expected_services": ["customer-portal", "order-service"], "required_facts": ["sessionStorage", "Idempotency-Key"], "required_considerations": [], "forbidden_assumptions": [], "reference_evidence": [{"path": "openwiki/checkout-flow.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/nagv/CommerceLens/blob/main/openwiki/checkout-flow.md", "sha256": "9755f56edb3556f4eecddbfea85a08562011f82cc6b4e5be8fa2150a43f18a3f"}, {"path": "openwiki/data-and-events.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/nagv/CommerceLens/blob/main/openwiki/data-and-events.md", "sha256": "5799bf7a4cc9bd04f8df976410e8c9946608d86f34461ff087b011b3a13c6922"}], "snapshot_version": "2026-11-09"}
